 "intro_html": "Ramen noodles get their bounce and yellow tint from an alkaline salt (kansui). The Momofuku trick: <b>bake ordinary baking soda</b> for an hour and it turns into a much stronger alkali (sodium carbonate). Dissolve it in the water, make a stiff dough, rest it, and roll it through a pasta machine. Use these for the <a href=\"ramen.html\">ramen</a> or the <a href=\"ginger-scallion-noodles.html\">ginger scallion noodles</a>.",
